{
  "name": "ADH kinetics: ethanol oxidation by yeast ADH1",
  "version": "2",
  "description": "Alcohol dehydrogenase 1 from Saccharomyces cerevisiae (strain ATCC 204508 / S288c) converts ethanol to acetaldehyde. Formation of NADH followed photometrically at 340 nm; the decrease of ethanol derived from it. Three starting concentrations spanning K_m (2, 8, 18 mM, K_m 17), 11 time points each over 20 min.\n\nSynthetic teaching dataset: the numbers come from a Michaelis-Menten simulation with added noise, not from a bench. The chemical and biological identifiers are real — the reaction from Rhea RHEA:25290, the enzyme from UniProt P00330.",
